## 3. The placebo and nocebo effects

The book discusses two important concepts:

### Placebo effect

Expectations and the context of treatment can influence how a person experiences certain symptoms, such as pain. This does not mean that belief alone cures an underlying disease.

### Nocebo effect

Negative expectations can contribute to unpleasant symptoms or make symptoms feel worse. This is one reason why communication between patients and healthcare professionals matters.

These are real areas of scientific study, but they do not establish every claim Lipton makes about consciousness and cellular control.&#x20;

