## 5. What science supports — and what to question

| Idea                                  | Scientific perspective                                                                       |
| ------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Environment affects biology           | Well established; environmental factors can influence cellular function and gene expression. |
| Stress can affect health              | Well established, although effects vary between people and circumstances.                    |
| Expectations can influence symptoms   | Supported by research on placebo and nocebo effects.                                         |
| Beliefs alone determine gene activity | Too broad; gene regulation is complex and influenced by many biological factors.             |
| Positive thinking can cure disease    | Not established. Positive thinking cannot replace evidence-based medical care.               |

The book is most useful when it encourages curiosity about biology, healthier habits, and constructive thinking. Some of its wider claims about quantum physics and consciousness are speculative and should not be treated as established scientific conclusions.&#x20;

